ution "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 8+11\\cdot (-11)+4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =32-121+12 \\\\  & =-77.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497741 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19b5771e-881c-5dc7-bd47-631de07881b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-31.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19b5771e-881c-5dc7-bd47-631de07881b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-31.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497699} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e3cec3a-81a2-544d-8588-a3c2224df3cf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497700}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ef62ae0b-9434-50fd-9674-89052980205a" :question/problem "If $a=⟨3.9,4.9,-5.9⟩$ and $b=⟨-5.6,1.8,3.2⟩,$ then $a\\cdot b=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =3.9\\cdot (-5.6)+4.9\\cdot 1.8+(-5.9)\\cdot 3.2 \\\\  & =-21.84+8.82-18.88 \\\\  & =-31.9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Dot Product Using the General Formula"}]}
